0393: SweetFramebuffer: kern.sweet_fb_regs also reads MDSS's own registers (HW_REV, UBWC_DEC_HW_VERSION, UBWC_STATIC), read only

0349's kern.sweet_fb_regs dumps the display engine from MDP TOP (0x5e01000) on. The registers that say how the
display decodes UBWC are MDSS's own, below it: HW_REV (+0x0), UBWC_DEC_HW_VERSION (+0x58), UBWC_STATIC
(+0x144), UBWC_CTRL_2 (+0x150), UBWC_PREDICTION_MODE (+0x154) (Linux v6.12 msm_mdss.c). Linux writes
UBWC_STATIC for this SoC family (sm6115_data: 0x11f with a 2.0 decoder), as does the phone's device tree
(qcom,sde-ubwc-static 0x11f); this kernel does not. The dump gains a first block "MDSS" (0x5e00000, 0x160
bytes); VIG0's entry, which the boot copy uses, moves to index 3 (SWEET_FBR_VIG0). Nothing is written.

Measured on the phone (one boot): +0x00 0x600a0000, +0x58 0x20000000, +0x144 0x00000000, +0x150 0x00000001:
neither the bootloader nor the kernel sets UBWC_STATIC. Read with: sysctl kern.sweet_fb_regs | head -14.

